        <reference anchor="RFC2048" target="https://www.rfc-editor.org/info/rfc2048" quoteTitle="true" derivedAnchor="RFC2048">
          <front>
            <title>Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) Part Four: Registration Procedures</title>
            <author fullname="N. Freed" initials="N." surname="Freed"/>
            <author fullname="J. Klensin" initials="J." surname="Klensin"/>
            <author fullname="J. Postel" initials="J." surname="Postel"/>
            <date month="November" year="1996"/>
            <abstract>
              <t indent="0">This set of documents, collectively called the Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions, or MIME, redefines the format of messages. This fourth document, RFC 2048, specifies various IANA registration procedures for some MIME facilities. This document specifies an Internet Best Current Practices for the Internet Community, and requests discussion and suggestions for improvements.</t>
            </abstract>
          </front>
          <seriesInfo name="RFC" value="2048"/>
          <seriesInfo name="DOI" value="10.17487/RFC2048"/>
        </reference>
